# PRP — Unit tests test/settingsLoader.test.ts (merge, trust, never-throw)

## Goal

**Feature Goal**: Ship a passing `test/settingsLoader.test.ts` that is the authoritative regression guard for the `loadMulliganSettings` contract built in P1.M1.T1.S1: project-local-over-global top-level REPLACE precedence, the strict `isTrusted===true` trust gate, the never-throws / warn-and-skip discipline on malformed input, and the `undefined`-when-absent → `DEFAULT_CONFIG` consumer contract. Every behavioral branch of the loader is pinned by exactly one focused `it()`, so any future regression in `src/settingsLoader.ts` (e.g. an accidental deep-merge, a dropped trust gate, a thrown error on bad JSON) turns a specific assertion red.

**Deliverable**: A single new test file at `test/settingsLoader.test.ts` (sibling of `test/config.test.ts` and `test/log.test.ts`). It imports `loadMulliganSettings` from `../src/settingsLoader.js` and `DEFAULT_CONFIG` + `validateConfig` from `../src/config.js`, uses `vi.mock("node:os")` to redirect `homedir()` at a fresh tmp dir per test, writes fixtures via `node:fs` + `os.tmpdir()`, and covers branches (a)–(h) of the work-item contract plus the pinned non-object `.mulligan` behavior and the two consumer-contract assertions.

**Success Definition**: `npx vitest run test/settingsLoader.test.ts` passes with all cases green; `npm test` stays green (zero regressions across the full suite); `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` passes. The test asserts the LOCAL value (NOT the global) in the both-present case (the precedence regression guard), asserts the local file is never read under `isTrusted:false` AND `isTrusted:undefined`, asserts exactly one `console.warn` per malformed file, and wraps adversarial inputs in `expect(()=>...).not.toThrow()`.

## Why

- **BUG-001 (critical, parent milestone P1.M1):** the whole config surface is inert today because the factory never calls `setConfig`. P1.M1.T1.S1 built the pure disk-reader (`src/settingsLoader.ts`); P1.M1.T2.S1 will wire `setConfig(loadMulliganSettings(...))` at factory load + every `session_start`. THIS task (S2) is the regression guard that locks the loader's merge/trust/never-throw semantics in place BEFORE and AFTER that wiring lands — so a future edit cannot silently re-introduce an inert-config path (deep-merge, dropped trust gate, or a thrown error that breaks factory/session load).
- **Why a dedicated test file (not folded into config.test.ts):** `settingsLoader.ts` is a STATELESS pure leaf (no `cachedConfig` module-scope state), so it does NOT need `vi.resetModules()` — unlike `config.test.ts`, which must reset modules because `config.ts` caches `cachedConfig` at module scope (external_deps.md §9). Keeping the loader's tests in their own file avoids the `vi.resetModules()` dance and mirrors the repo's one-test-file-per-source-module convention (log.test.ts↔log.ts, tokens.test.ts↔tokens.ts, etc.).
- **Precedence is the load-bearing regression guard:** spec/09 §1 mandates project-local WINS via top-level REPLACE (NOT deep-merge). design_decisions.md BUG-001 "Rejected alternatives" EXPLICITLY forbids deep-merge (it introduces ambiguity on partial `rewind` blocks, and `validateConfig` already fills sub-key defaults). The both-present test asserts the LOCAL object verbatim (`{b:2}`, NOT `{a:1,b:2}`) so a future deep-merge mistake fails loudly.

## What

### Public API under test (built in S1 — do NOT modify it)
```ts
export type LoadMulliganSettingsOptions = { cwd?: string; isTrusted?: boolean };
export function loadMulliganSettings(opts?: LoadMulliganSettingsOptions): unknown;

```
Behavior (VERIFIED against the shipped src/settingsLoader.ts):
1. GLOBAL: `join(homedir(), ".pi", "agent", "settings.json")` — read unconditionally; take ONLY the `mulligan` own-key (ignore `packages`/`defaultModel`/etc.).
2. LOCAL: `join(opts.cwd, ".pi", "settings.json")` — read ONLY when `opts.isTrusted === true` (strict `=== true`) AND `typeof opts.cwd === "string"`.
3. MERGE = top-level REPLACE: if LOCAL has a `mulligan` own-key (ANY value incl. `null`), the LOCAL value REPLACES the global entirely. Else the global value (if any).
4. Return: the merged `mulligan` (type `unknown`) or `undefined` when neither file has a `mulligan` key. Non-object `.mulligan` returned AS-IS (config.ts:validateConfig coerces).
5. NEVER throws: ENOENT/EACCES/EISDIR → silently skip; malformed JSON (incl. JSONC `//` comments → SyntaxError) → `console.warn("[mulligan] settings: <path> unreadable: <msg>")` (itself try/catch-wrapped) then skip; non-record top-level → no `mulligan` key → contributes nothing.

### Success Criteria
- [ ] Every contract branch (a)–(h) below has at least one focused `it()`.
- [ ] Both-present case asserts the LOCAL value verbatim (NOT deep-merged) — the precedence regression guard.
- [ ] `isTrusted:false` AND `isTrusted:undefined` both skip the local read (two sub-asserts or two cases).
- [ ] Malformed-JSON cases assert EXACTLY ONE `console.warn` per malformed file, with the mandated prefix and the offending path, via `vi.spyOn(console,"warn").mockImplementation(()=>{})` + `warn.mockRestore()` in `finally`.
- [ ] Non-object `.mulligan` (42, 'off', null) returned AS-IS — pinned in one case.
- [ ] Consumer contract: `loadMulliganSettings()===undefined` → `validateConfig(undefined)` deepEquals `DEFAULT_CONFIG`; AND `{mulligan:null}` → returns null → `validateConfig(null)===DEFAULT_CONFIG`.
- [ ] Never-throws: adversarial inputs (bad cwd dir, no opts, isTrusted without cwd, cwd without isTrusted) wrapped in `expect(()=>...).not.toThrow()`.
- [ ] `vi.mock("node:os")` redirects `homedir()` so the GLOBAL path is hermetic (no read of the real `~/.pi/agent/settings.json`).

