## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- ❌ Don't fold this into config.test.ts or add vi.resetModules() — the loader is stateless; resetModules is only for config.ts's cachedConfig.
- ❌ Don't read the REAL ~/.pi/agent/settings.json — always vi.mock("node:os") to point homedir at a tmp dir, or tests are machine-dependent and flaky.
- ❌ Don't assert deep-merge in the both-present case — spec/09 §1 mandates top-level REPLACE; assert the LOCAL object verbatim.
- ❌ Don't use truthiness to detect the mulligan key — {mulligan:null} IS present (hasOwnProperty); your null-wins case must expect null.
- ❌ Don't forget warn.mockRestore() in a finally — a swallowed warn leaks into later tests.
- ❌ Don't assert console.warn fires on a MISSING file — ENOENT is silent; only malformed-JSON/EACCES/EISDIR warn.
- ❌ Don't modify src/settingsLoader.ts, src/config.ts, or src/index.ts (scope boundaries — S1 / P1.M1.T2.S1 own them).
- ❌ Don't call setConfig in this test (it mutates cachedConfig and couples a stateless test to config.ts's cache).
- ❌ Don't import @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent into the test (the loader is Pi-free; the test should be too).
